  "status": "Native metadata invariants qualified and candidate 10 prepared. Complete RPM/LTO, actual patched Wasm execution and native ARM remain gates. No exception requested.",
  "upstream_fix": "https://chromium.googlesource.com/v8/v8/+/a548b49ac38290fa2cf449117e19f872d0f3c7f5",
  "root_cause": "Wasm pipeline ignored CodeGenerator assembly failure, while cloning merge blocks could multiply deoptimization points. Release builds also omitted metadata index/ID and restored-value-kind checks. The metadata allocation narrows size_t to int without a visible bound, explaining the LTO allocation warning.",
  "fix": "Backport upstream no-cloning and release metadata/assembly checks. Additionally enforce the successful assembly invariant of zero-based IDs through 16384 before narrowing the count. This caps successful counts at 16385. Compiler and runtime feature policies are unchanged.",
  "backport_adaptations": [
    "This older V8 version has no separate is_simd128_reg branch; the upstream check in the existing fp-register SIMD case is retained.",
    "Its SIMD stack representation uses int64x2 rather than Simd128::int64x2; only the upstream kind check is added.",
    "The explicit entry-count check is an additional local invariant before narrowing, not an upstream hunk."
  ],
  "coverage": {
    "native_checks_per_execution": 1969500,
    "normal_and_memory_runs": 4,
    "native_types": "Unchanged generator allocation/fill prefix with a typed surrounding-state adapter; actual OwnedVector, BytecodeOffset, WasmDeoptEntry, WasmDeoptView, literal objects and complete serializer implementation.",
    "positive": "Counts 0,1,2,17,16384,16385; translation lengths 0,1,5; every entry and four literal types round-trip. Both variants run normally and under Valgrind.",
    "negative": "Original release source accepts six invalid states. Corrected source rejects failed generation, excess count, duplicate ID, negative eager count, inconsistent eager count and an out-of-range logical entry. The baseline out-of-range backing allocation remains valid to avoid undefined behavior in the test itself.",
    "memory": "All four positive executions pass. Both Valgrind runs have zero errors and all 479 allocations freed.",
    "compiler": "Native controls and actual standalone generator files compile without diagnostics in both variants. The smaller builds do not reproduce the full LTO allocation warning.",
    "upstream_baseline": "All 31 unchanged version-matched Wasm deoptimization scripts pass using the candidate-9 installed Node RPM. The Node adapter supplies only file execute and print; V8 intrinsics and original flags remain.",
    "packaging": "21 helper/metadata tests and 17 dependency tests pass. All 21 patches apply without fuzz, and seven backport files match qualified proposed sources."
  },
  "limits": [
    "The generator state adapter does not execute instruction assembly or prove the branch-cloning change. Those require the patched complete build and upstream runtime suites.",
    "Standalone generator compilation does not exercise full-build LTO; disappearance of the exact allocation warning must be verified in candidate 10.",
    "Only x86_64 native controls are complete; native ARM compilation and runtime remain required.",
    "No speculative INT_MAX-sized allocation is performed. The new bound is tested at the real successful assembly maximum and its immediate successor."
  ],
